      "problem": "Convert the expression $\\ln{3} \\approx 1.1$ to its equivalent exponential form.",
      "worked_solution": "The natural logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\ln{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = e^x$\n\nIf we compare $\\ln{3} \\approx 1.1$ with $\\ln{a} = x,$ we get $a = 3$ and $x = 1.1.$\n\nTherefore, the approximation $\\ln{3} \\approx 1.1$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\ne^{1.1} \\approx 3 .\n$$",
